{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1152","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F1. Neko Rules the Catniverse (Small Version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"7 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem is same as the next one, but has smaller constraints"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aki is playing a new video game. In the video game, he will control Neko, the giant cat, to fly between planets in the Catniverse."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ planets in the Catniverse, numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. At the beginning of the game, Aki chooses the planet where Neko is initially located. Then Aki performs $$$k - 1$$$ moves, where in each move Neko is moved from the current planet $$$x$$$ to some other planet $$$y$$$ such that:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Planet $$$y$$$ is not visited yet. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\leq y \\leq x + m$$$ (where $$$m$$$ is a fixed constant given in the input) "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This way, Neko will visit exactly $$$k$$$ different planets. Two ways of visiting planets are called different if there is some index $$$i$$$ such that the $$$i$$$-th planet visited in the first way is different from the $$$i$$$-th planet visited in the second way."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What is the total number of ways to visit $$$k$$$ planets this way? Since the answer can be quite large, print it modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$k$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le \\min(n, 12)$$$, $$$1 \\le m \\le 4$$$) — the number of planets in the Catniverse, the number of planets Neko needs to visit and the said constant $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print exactly one integer — the number of different ways Neko can visit exactly $$$k$$$ planets. Since the answer can be quite large, print it modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n9\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 5 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n120\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n100 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n100\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there are $$$4$$$ ways Neko can visit all the planets:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\rightarrow 3 \\rightarrow 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\rightarrow 1 \\rightarrow 2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, there are $$$9$$$ ways Neko can visit exactly $$$2$$$ planets:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\rightarrow 2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\rightarrow 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\rightarrow 3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\rightarrow 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\rightarrow 2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\rightarrow 4$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$4 \\rightarrow 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$4 \\rightarrow 2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$4 \\rightarrow 3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, with $$$m = 4$$$, Neko can visit all the planets in any order, so there are $$$5! = 120$$$ ways Neko can visit all the planets."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth example, Neko only visit exactly $$$1$$$ planet (which is also the planet he initially located), and there are $$$100$$$ ways to choose the starting planet for Neko."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F1","problemCode":"1152F1","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1152/problem/F1"}